=== O5. Lemma O9 (Euclidean Z2): |A|^2 in eigen-coordinates; its O(4)-average is proportional to |Rm|^2   [150 s]
  [ 28] n = 3, base (3,0), Z2, lambda = 0, c_H = 2, c_V = 3, y0 = diag(1/2, 2, 3): brute-force s_Y = R/c_H + s_F - |A|^2 with |A|^2 = c_V/(4 c_H^2) sum_{ijkl} R_klij^2 (u_k/u_l + u_l/u_k - 2): True
  [ 29] n = 4, Euclidean: the space of algebraic curvature tensors has dim 20 = 10 (Weyl) + 9 (Ric_0) + 1 (True); for Q_u(R) = sum R_klij^2 f_kl at three random diagonal u, tr(Q|_V)/dim V is the same on all three components (= sum_(k!=l) f_kl / 12 = 2633/1080, 583/72, 317/288), so avg_O(4) Q_u = (sum f/12) |Rm|^2, and sum_(k!=l) f_kl = 2 (tr u tr u^-1 - n^2): True

